# Test Architecture

## Core patterns
- Follow the Factory/Strategy design: use `DriverFactory` to resolve an `AutomationDriver`.
- Test classes extend `BaseTest` for setup/teardown and reporting hooks.
- Keep tests orchestration-only; driver/strategy classes handle implementation details.

## Suite taxonomy
- Use TestNG groups: `smoke`, `regression`, `web`, `api`, `mobile` as applicable.
- Align suites with Gradle tasks: `webTest`, `apiTest`, `mobileTest`, `smokeTest`, `regressionTest`.

## Configuration and data
- Read environment and execution mode via `ConfigManager`.
- Externalize locators and test data under `src/test/resources`.
- Avoid hardcoded endpoints/URLs in tests; use locator keys and config properties.

## Example
```java
@Test(groups = {"smoke", "api"}, description = "Verify GET orders endpoint returns 200")
public void shouldGetOrdersSuccessfully() {
    ApiDriverStrategy api = (ApiDriverStrategy) driver;
    ApiResponse response = api.get("orders.endpoint");
    Assert.assertEquals(response.getStatusCode(), 200);
}
```
